INSERT INTO characters (slug,name,team,creator,owner_id,tags,appears_in,data,url_slug,status,updated_at,created_at) VALUES
('umbilical','Umbilical','minion','legitch',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"umbilical","name":"Umbilical","team":"minion","ability":"The Demon has a 2nd Demon ability (they know which), but cannot kill with it. You might register falsely to marked characters.","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"The Umbilical Baby (SCP-395) is a telepathic and hungry fetus which acts as the 2nd vessel for the Demon... also, I think it just moved.","summaryBullets":["The Demon gets a 2nd Demon ability from the script. It is not the same ability they already have.","For all intents and purposes, the Demon has the 2nd ability overlapped on-top of their own.","When the 2nd Demon ability triggers something upon it performing a kill, it also triggers upon the original Demon ability making the kill.","If any character has an ability that would detect or affect a good player that is marked on the script, then the Umbilical will register as good to that character. For those abilities that then detect Townsfolk or Outsiders, then the Umbilical might register as a specific Townsfolk or Outsider to that player, but they''ll never register as a Minion."],"howToRun":["On the script, place a mark on characters whose abilities you want to be susceptible to the Umbilical''s misregistration.","While setting up the game, before putting character tokens in the bag, decide what the 2nd Demon will be, and respect the setup effects of their ability. Put the 2nd Demon''s character token in the center of the left side of the Grimoire.","While preparing the first night, put the Umbilical''s **USES 2ND ABILITY** reminder token by the Demon''s character token. Also, move the 2nd Demon''s character token by the Demon''s character token - if the current medium of play is unable to allow for this, you may instead replace the Umbilical''s token with the 2nd Demon token, but marking them with the **IS THE Umbilical** reminder, indicating they have not changed characters from the Umbilical into the 2nd Demon.","During the first night, wake the Demon. Show them the **THIS CHARACTER SELECTED YOU** info token, the Umbilical''s token, then the 2nd Demon''s character token. Put the Demon to sleep. The Demon now has the 2nd Demon''s ability, and has it overlapped ontop of their existing ability. However, the Demon cannot use this 2nd Demon ability to kill additional targets.","Each time the Umbilical is targeted by an ability directly marked on the script that detects or affects good characters or the Demon, the Umbilical will register as that. Do whatever is appropriate, such as showing a good character token, nodding, giving finger signals, or allowing an ability to work that would normally only affect good, Townsfolk, Outsider, or Demon players."],"tips":["It''s recommended that you mark half the Townsfolk whose abilities are susceptible to directly misregistering the Umbilical when targeted.","Players should read into the intent of this character as having a Demon''s secondary ability stapled seamlessly ontop of the current Demon, based off the law of ''rules-as-intended''. You rarely should any bootleg interactions with the Umbilical cause of this when building your script.","**Optional rule:** as you''re placing marks by the characters whose abilities that will register the Umbilical as good & a good character, you may place Demon character icons by the Umbilical to indicate these are the only Demons the Umbilical will use for the 2nd Demon ability, and also place marks on the Demons that you want to indicate will never be in-play, and will only be used for a potential 2nd Demon ability."],"quote":"Are you my mommy?","iconBy":"le_nuberto","jinxes":[{"name":"Al-Hadikhia","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Al-Hadikhia as their second ability.","id":"alhadikhia"},{"name":"Kazali","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Kazali as their second ability.","id":"kazali"},{"name":"Legion","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Legion as their second ability.","id":"legion"},{"name":"Leviathan","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Leviathan as their second ability.","id":"leviathan"},{"name":"Lil'' Monsta","align":"evil","text":"The 2nd Demon ability is attached to Lil'' Monsta at all times & cannot change. The Demon cannot have the Lil'' Monsta as their second ability.","id":"lilmonsta"},{"name":"Ojo","align":"evil","text":"If the Demon has the Ojo as their second ability, they instead choose characters instead of players with their ability.","id":"ojo"},{"name":"Riot","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Riot as their second ability.","id":"riot"},{"name":"Shabaloth","align":"evil","text":"If the Demon has the Shabaloth as their 2nd Demon ability, they can only use it to kill one player per night, and that player is the only one that may be regurgitated.","id":"shabaloth"},{"name":"Yaggababble","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Yaggababble as their second ability.","id":"yaggababble"},{"name":"Watislujv","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Watislujv as their second ability.","slug":"watislujv"},{"name":"Abysewhell","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Abysewhell as their second ability.","slug":"abysewhell"},{"name":"Cespholopod","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Cespholopod as their second ability.","slug":"cespholopod"},{"name":"Lettucbaken","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Lettucbaken as their second ability.","slug":"lettucbaken"},{"name":"▼","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the ▽ as their second ability.","slug":"scp-1936"},{"name":"Eyeceue","align":"evil","text":"The 2nd Demon ability is attached to ''the Demon'' at all times. The Demon cannot have the Eyeceue as their second ability.","slug":"eyeceue"},{"name":"xX_2662_Xx","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the xX_2662_Xx as their second ability.","slug":"xx-2662-xx"},{"name":"O. Horseman","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the O. Horsemen as their second ability.","slug":"o-horseman"},{"name":"Bloodwrite","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Bloodwrite as their second ability.","id":"bloodwrite_hblreleased"},{"name":"Kukalpa","align":"evil","text":"If the Demon has the Kukalpa as their 2nd Demon ability, their primary ability will always be active, even while dead.","id":"kukalpa_hblreleased"},{"name":"Matsuraid","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Matsuraid as their second ability.","id":"matsuraid_hblreleased"},{"name":"Au’Wre","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Au''Wre as their second ability.","id":"auwre_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Cawthane","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Cawthane as their second ability.","id":"cawthane_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Ketos","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Ketos as their second ability.","id":"ketos_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Obscrul","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Obscrul as their second ability.","id":"obscrul_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Schai","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Schai as their second ability.","id":"schai"},{"name":"Midnight","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Midnight as their second ability.","id":"midnight"},{"name":"Tao Tie","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Tao Tie as their second ability.","id":"taotie_festival_of_lanterns"},{"name":"Switchblame","align":"evil","text":"The Demon cannot have the Switchblame as their second ability.","id":"switchblame_mistfitsreleased"},{"name":"Cataphractos","align":"evil","text":"If the Demon has the Cataphractos as their 2nd Demon ability, they can only use it to kill one player per night if they neighbour an alive Minion.","id":"cataphractos_mistfitsreleased"}],"firstNight":8.395,"otherNight":0,"reminders":["Uses 2nd ability"],"remindersGlobal":["Is the Umbilical"],"setup":true,"firstNightReminder":"Wake the Demon, show them the ''This character selected you'' card, show the Umbilical''s token and the character token of the 2nd Demon.","art":"art/umbilical.png","jsonId":"umbilical_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/umbilical','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('tooth-fairy','Tooth Fairy','minion','legitch',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"tooth-fairy","name":"Tooth Fairy","team":"minion","ability":"1 player has a tooth, even if not in-play. Each night, holders can pass it; every 2nd time a good holder is dead, a player dies.","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"The Tooth Fairy (SCP-478) is a pest that infects its host with a beautiful thing - more teeth! WE ALL LOVE HAVING TEETH!","summaryBullets":["A player - typically a good one - starts holding a tooth, and may decide for themselves to either keep holding onto it, or to pass it along.","Provided the Tooth Fairy is on the script, this tooth will always arrive.","Holders of the tooth wake after the Demon kills and choose who keeps it by nodding their head ''no'' or by pointing to a player.","Players who receive the tooth from another player know who that player is - the Storyteller only acts as the middle man for interaction of changing owners.","If the Storyteller thinks it is funny, they may give this player the Tooth reminder token. There isn''t much of a reason for players to be interrogating others into coaxing the tooth, as players who receive the tooth know gave it to them, and evil players are in pursuit for whoever is currently holding the tooth.","Every other time the Tooth Fairy''s tooth is given to a dead good player, the current good holder dies holding it, or a good dead holder doesn''t pass it, a player {{i|(typically a Townsfolk)}} dies tonight.","However, these killings do not occur if the Tooth Fairy is not actually in-play, and thus, the Tooth does nothing but only to disseminate if the Tooth Fairy is in-play or not.","Any player can be killed by the Tooth Fairy, including Outsiders, and even other Minions if the Storyteller deems it necessary to keep the game stable."],"howToRun":["While preparing the first night, put the Tooth Fairy''s **TOOTH** reminder token by any character token. If you choose, you may procure the object that will physically serve as **THE TOOTH** for players to hold on their persons {{i|(this may be a toy tooth, silver tooth, or even the Tooth reminder token if you can remember who is currently holding it at all times)}}.","Each night, wake the player holding **THE TOOTH**. Show them the **THIS CHARACTER SELECTED YOU** info token, the Tooth Fairy''s character token, then procure **THE TOOTH**. They either shake their head no or point at any player. Put them to sleep. If the Tooth Fairy is marked with the **KILLING** reminder token, you choose any player. The chosen player {{i|dies}} - mark them with the **DEAD** reminder.","If the player holding **THE TOOTH** chose a player, they pass it to a new holder - move **THE TOOTH** to the player they chose. Wake the new holder of **THE TOOTH**, show them the **THIS CHARACTER SELECTED YOU** info token, the Tooth Fairy''s character token, point at the previous holder, then procure **THE TOOTH**.","Whilst the Tooth Fairy is in-play, at any time, if the holder of **THE TOOTH** dies and is good, **THE TOOTH** is passed along to a dead good holder, or a good dead holder of the **THE TOOTH** does not pass it when they could, if the Tooth Fairy is marked **ODD**, remove it and mark the Tooth Fairy with the **KILLING** reminder token; otherwise if the Tooth Fairy isn''t marked with the **ODD** reminder token, mark them with it."],"quote":"Teeth, teeth, teeth! Gums, gums, gums! Bleed, bleed, bleed! Splash, splash, splash! We love teeth! Teeth, teeth, teeth!","iconBy":"le_nuberto","customBoxes":[{"title":"In the almanac JSON","content":"**First night:** Wake the current holder of the Tooth, show them the ''This character selected you'' card, show the Tooth Fairy''s token, then procure the tooth for them. They either show the ''no'' head signal, or point to a player. The chosen player now holds the tooth and is now marked ''Tooth''. Wake the chosen player, show them the ''This character selected you'' token, the Tooth Fairy''s token, then point to the previous holder and procure the tooth for them."},{"title":"Alternative JSON & How to Run (Older)","content":"If you want to use the older version of this character that poisoned instead of killed, use this JSON.\n\nWhile preparing the first night, put the Tooth Fairy''s **TOOTH** reminder token by any good player''s character token. If you choose, you may procure the object that will physically serve as **THE TOOTH** for players to hold on their persons {{i|(this may be a toy tooth, silver tooth, or even the Tooth reminder token if you can remember who is currently holding it at all times)}}.\n\nEach night, wake the player holding **THE TOOTH**. Show them the **THIS CHARACTER SELECTED YOU** info token, the Tooth Fairy''s character token, then procure **THE TOOTH**. They either shake their head no or point at any player. Put them to sleep.\n\nIf the player holding **THE TOOTH** chose a player, they pass it to a new holder - move **THE TOOTH** to the player they chose. Wake the new holder of **THE TOOTH**, show them the **THIS CHARACTER SELECTED YOU** info token, the Tooth Fairy''s character token, point at the previous holder, then procure **THE TOOTH**.\n\nAt any time, if the holder of **THE TOOTH** dies and is good, **THE TOOTH** is passed along to a dead good holder, or a good dead holder of the **THE TOOTH** does not pass it when they could, if the Tooth Fairy is marked **ODD**, remove it and a player becomes poisoned - put the **POISONED** reminder token by the chosen player''s character token; otherwise if the Tooth Fairy isn''t marked with the **ODD** reminder token, mark them with it.\n\n**Tooth Fairy █~** (Minion)\n1 good player has a permanent tooth; holders can pass it each night. Every 2nd time a good holder is dead, a player is poisoned.\n\n**First night:** Wake the current holder of the Tooth, show them the ''This character selected you'' card, show the Tooth Fairy''s token, then procure the tooth for them. They either show the ''no'' head signal, or point to a player. The chosen player now holds the tooth and is now marked ''Tooth''. Wake the chosen player, show them the ''This character selected you'' token, the Tooth Fairy''s token, then point to the previous holder and procure the tooth for them.\n**Other nights:** Wake the current holder of the Tooth even if the Tooth Fairy isn''t currently alive, show them the ''This character selected you'' card, show the Tooth Fairy''s token, then procure the tooth. They either show the ''no'' head signal, or point to a player. The chosen player now holds the tooth and is now marked ''Tooth''. Wake the chosen player, show them the ''This character selected you'' token, the Tooth Fairy''s token, then point to the previous holder and procure the tooth for them.\n**Reminders:** Odd, Poisoned, Poisoned, Poisoned, Poisoned, Poisoned, Tooth\n**Credit:** Ability: @legitch. Image: @le_nuberto"}],"firstNight":71.478,"otherNight":54.478,"reminders":["Odd","Killing","Dead"],"remindersGlobal":["Tooth"],"setup":false,"firstNightReminder":"Wake the current holder of the Tooth, show them the ''This character selected you'' card, show the Tooth Fairy''s token, then procure the tooth for them.  They either show the ''no'' head signal, or point to a player. The chosen player now holds the tooth and is now marked ''Tooth''. Wake the chosen player, show them the ''This character selected you'' token, the Tooth Fairy''s token, then point to the previous holder and procure the tooth for them.","otherNightReminder":"Wake the current holder of the Tooth even if the Tooth Fairy isn''t currently alive, show them the ''This character selected you'' card, show the Tooth Fairy''s token, then procure the tooth. They either show the ''no'' head signal, or point to a player. The chosen player now holds the tooth and is now marked ''Tooth''. Wake the chosen player, show them the ''This character selected you'' token, the Tooth Fairy''s token, then point to the previous holder and procure the tooth for them. If the Tooth Fairy is in-play and Tooth has been held by a dead good player since then on an other instance: Choose a player not protected from dying tonight. That player dies.","art":"art/tooth-fairy.png","jsonId":"toothfairy_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/tooth-fairy','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now'));
